      },
      {
         "id": "SECTION_introduction",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "<p><h3>Introduction</h3>We learned that when we cannot count using only our fingers, we can ask other people for help. But sometimes this is still not enough (<htcite0>).</p><p><table class=\"tawapukllay\"><tr><th colspan=\"2\">First person</th><th colspan=\"2\">Second person</th><th colspan=\"2\">Third person</th><th>Fourth person</th></tr>  <tr><td><img id=\"img5900\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('img5900', '0%')\" /></td><td><img id=\"img5901\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('img5901', '0%')\" /></td><td><img id=\"img5902\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('img5902', '0%')\" /></td><td><img id=\"img5903\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('img5903', '0%')\" /></td><td><img id=\"img5904\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('img5904', '0%')\" /></td><td><img id=\"img5905\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('img5905', '0%')\" /></td><td><img id=\"img5906\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('img5906', '0%')\" /></td></tr></table></p><p class=\"desc\"><b>Table 1</b>: Counting with a team.</p><p><center><div class=\"first_steps_reflection_parent\"><div class=\"first_steps_reflection question_mark\">?</div><div class=\"first_steps_reflection\"><b>Reflection 1: Hands and numbers</b><br />Observing <b>Table 1</b>, how would you replace hands with numbers?</div></div></center></p>",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "cc8c1467-a6af-4f9c-ba60-ab6df35aba05",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "Además de los Dedos",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2024",
                        "month": "07",
                        "day": "23"
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": [
                  {
                     "type": "gregory",
                     "year": "2024",
                     "month": "-1",
                     "day": "-1"
                  }
               ],
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "A table showing six hands with all fingers raised and one with only two fingers raised.",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "SECTION_limits",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "<p><h3>The limits</h3>To answer the first reflection, we need to find the limits of our numbers. Use the arrows to check the possible values we can have with decimal numbers:</p><p><table id=\"yupana0\" class=\"tawapukllay\"><tr><th colspan=\"4\"><i>Yupana</i></th><th>Left hand</th><th>Righjt hand</th><th>Hindu-arabic</th><th>Arrows</th></tr> <tr id=\"tf1\"><td id=\"tc1f1\"></td> <td id=\"tc2f1\"></td> <td id=\"tc3f1\"></td> <td id=\"tc4f1\"></td><td id=\"tc5f1\"><img onclick=\"htImageZoom('leftHandImg0', '0%')\" id=\"leftHandImg0\" /></td><td id=\"tc6f1\"><img onclick=\"htImageZoom('rightHandImg0', '0%')\" id=\"rightHandImg0\" /></td><td id=\"tc7f1\">&nbsp;</td><td> <i class=\"fa-solid fa-caret-up upArrowWithFA\" id=\"traineeUp0\"></i>  <i class=\"fa-solid fa-caret-down downArrowWithFA\" id=\"traineeDown0\"></i></td></tr></table>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p class=\"desc\"><b>Table 2</b>: Representation of a <i>Yupana</i> line according to Poma de Ayala (<htcite0> ; <htcite1>). CSS inspired by source code available on W3Schools (<htcite2>).</p><p><center><div class=\"first_steps_reflection_parent\"><div class=\"first_steps_reflection question_mark\">?</div><div class=\"first_steps_reflection\"><b>Reflection 2: The limits</b><br />When can we raise all fingers to represent a number?</div></div></center></p><p>The first step to answer this reflection is to review what we learned:</p><p><ul><li>When we click the up arrow (green arrow), the numbers increase up to 9.</li><li>When we click the down arrow (blue arrow), the numbers decrease down to 0.</li></ul></p><p>We can see that values go up to nine (9) at most and go down to zero (0) at least. These are the limits for each position of a number in the decimal system, and we must respect them.</p><p>Look at <b>Table 1</b>. When we needed help to count with our hands, other people stood beside us and raised their fingers. We can do the same with numbers, respecting their limits:</p>",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "a62b520a-f443-4d83-ab51-b99c9a46dab8",
                     "text": "Prem, Dhavit",
                     "page": "pp. 355",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2018",
                        "month": "04",
                        "day": "01"
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 0,
                     "uuid": "f5b74f18-0bc4-46d2-8a5c-64dd80b74dd1",
                     "text": "Poma de Ayala, Felipe Guaman",
                     "page": "pp. 361 - 362",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "1615",
                        "month": "02",
                        "day": "13"
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "48dd9187-7ecc-4f54-a387-d9ecc2497de3",
                     "text": "W3school",
                     "page": "",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2025",
                        "month": "01",
                        "day": "27"
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": [
                  {
                     "type": "gregory",
                     "year": "2018",
                     "month": "-1",
                     "day": "-1"
                  },
                  {
                     "type": "gregory",
                     "year": "1615",
                     "month": "-1",
                     "day": "-1"
                  }
               ],
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p><table class=\"tawapukllay\" id=\"yupana1\"><tr><th colspan=\"2\">Second person</th><th colspan=\"2\">First person</th><th>Hindu-Arabic</th><th>Hindu-Arabic</th><th>Arrows</th></tr>  <tr><td><img onclick=\"htImageZoom('leftHandImg2', '0%')\" id=\"leftHandImg2\" /></td><td><img onclick=\"htImageZoom('rightHandImg2', '0%')\" id=\"rightHandImg2\" /></td><td><img onclick=\"htImageZoom('leftHandImg1', '0%')\" id=\"leftHandImg1\" /></td><td><img onclick=\"htImageZoom('rightHandImg1', '0%')\" id=\"rightHandImg1\" /></td><td id=\"tc5f1\"></td><td id=\"tc6f1\"></td><td><i class=\"fa-solid fa-caret-up upArrowWithFA\" id=\"traineeUp1\"></i>  <i class=\"fa-solid fa-caret-down downArrowWithFA\" id=\"traineeDown1\"></i></td></tr></table></p><p class=\"desc\"><b>Table 3</b>: The logic of numbers</p><p>The zero (0) represents the idea of emptiness (<htcite0>). So we do not write zeros on the left side of other numbers. But we can think that the zeros are there. With this in mind, when a position reaches the maximum (9), we add one to the next position and set the current position back to zero.</p><p>We could keep using the arrows to get numbers bigger than nineteen (19). But on this page, we will only look at these numbers. On the next pages, we will work with bigger numbers.</p>",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "576e4648-77fa-4a6d-9e51-9459ced964f3",
                     "text": "Musa, Auwalu",
                     "page": "pp. 44, 46 - 48",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2024",
                        "month": "05",
                        "day": "19"
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": [
                  {
                     "type": "gregory",
                     "year": "2014",
                     "month": "-1",
                     "day": "-1"
                  }
               ],
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "SECTION_mesoamerican",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "<p><h3>Extending the numerical system</h3>Besides the decimal system, indigenous peoples made another system, the vigesimal (<htcite0> ; <htcite1> ; <htcite2> ; <htcite3> ; <htcite4>). Its symbols can be linked to our toes. Below we show the relationship between this system and our fingers:</p><table class=\"tawapukllay\" id=\"yupana2\"><tr><th>Left hand</th><th>Right hand</th><th>Left foot</th><th>Right foot</th><th>Indigenous</th><th>Hindu-arabic</th></tr> </table><p class=\"desc\"><b>Table 4</b>: Hindu-Arabic Numbers and Their Relationship with Our Members.</p>",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "ad11b3b2-8cdf-4d71-9cb7-2ac241850945",
                     "text": "Casares Contreras, Orlando & Cetina, José & Cabrera, Venus Sarahí, , (ResearchGate)",
                     "page": "pp. 25 - 26",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2022",
                        "month": "07",
                        "day": "25"
                     }
                  },
                  {
